d intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le11ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Talking About Someone's Feelings and Reactions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You talk about feelings and reactions using adjectives."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\"> -ed </span> are used to describe how a person feels, like <span class=\"italic\">excited</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> amazed </span> or  interested</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\">-ing </span> are used to describe things and situations, like   <span class=\"italic\">exciting</span>,   <span class=\"italic\">amazing</span> or   <span class=\"italic\">interesting</span>.  These adjectives describe the   <span class=\"italic\">effect</span> something has on a person."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I set up my profile last night, and I've already received a few messages. I'm really excited!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "This is exciting!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Swipe right if you find someone interesting, or swipe left if you're not interested! "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking for Help or Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " There are several ways to ask for help in English. You can use polite and casual language to do this.  Let's look at one particular structure for asking for help."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the structure:<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Can</span>/ <span class=\"strong\">Could</span>/ <span class=\"strong\">Do</span> +  <span class=\"strong\">you</span> +  <span class=\"strong\">verb</span> +  <span class=\"strong\">me (optional)</span> +  <span class=\"strong\">Question word</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type